What is a Console Application in C#? -
------------------------------------
A Console Application is a text-based program that runs inside a black-and-white window called the console.

It doesn't have buttons, menus, or forms.

It takes input from the keyboard and gives output to the screen using text.

It's the best place to start learning C# programming.

Real Life Analogy:
Think of a Console App like talking to a friend using WhatsApp Chat (text only) — you type something, and it replies.
Later, we'll build GUI apps (like video calls or games), but we first learn chat-style!

Why We Use Console Apps for Learning?

Reason	                  Benefit
Simple and clean	  ->    Focus only on logic and code
Fast to test ideas	  ->    No need to build fancy UI
Lightweight     	  ->   Runs on all computers easily
Perfect for beginners ->	No distractions — only pure C#
